<title>MALAYSIA: GOVERNMENT LIST.</title>
<headline>GOVERNMENT LIST.</headline>
<text>
<p>MALAYSIA GOVERNMENT LIST (970502)</p>
<p>Supreme Head of State (Yang Di-Pertuan Agong)</p>
<p>(chosen for five year term 26 Apr 94, installed</p>
<p>     22 Sep 94)......Sultan TUANKU JA'AFAR Tuanku Abdul Rahman</p>
<p>				 - - - - - - -</p>
<p>NATIONAL FRONT (COALITION) GOVERNMENT (Formed 03 May 95)</p>
<p> Prime Minister.........MAHATHIR Mohamad (UMNO)</p>
<p>(also Minister of Home Affairs)</p>
<p>Deputy Prime Minister.....ANWAR Ibrahim (UMNO)</p>
<p>(also Minister of Finance)</p>
<p> Ministers in the PM's Department........ABANG Abu Bakar (PBB)</p>
<p>						 ABDUL Hamid Othman (UMNO)</p>
<p>							   (one post vacant)</p>
<p>MINISTERS:</p>
<p> Agriculture................SULAIMAN Daud (PBB)</p>
<p>Culture Arts &amp; Tourism.SABBARUDDIN Chik (UMNO)</p>
<p> Defence................SYED Hamid Albar (UMNO)</p>
<p> Education.............NAJIB Abdul Razak (UMNO)</p>
<p> Energy, Telecommunications &amp; Post...........LEO Moggie (PBDS)</p>
<p>Entrepreuner Development &amp; Domestic</p>
<p>Trade &amp; Consumer Affairs (Acting)...MUSTAPA Mohamed (UMNO)</p>
<p> Finance..............See Deputy Prime Minister</p>
<p> Foreign...........ABDULLAH AHMAD Badawi (UMNO)</p>
<p> Health......CHUA Jui Meng (MCA)</p>
<p> Home.........See Prime Minister</p>
<p>Housing &amp; Local Government.TING Chew Peh (MCA)</p>
<p> Human Resources...............LIM Ah Lek (MCA)</p>
<p> Information..............MOHAMED Rahmat (UMNO)</p>
<p> International Trade &amp; Industry............RAFIDAH Aziz (UMNO)</p>
<p> Land &amp; Cooperative Development...............OSU Sukam (UMNO)</p>
<p> National Unity &amp; Development.............ZALEHA Ismail (UMNO)</p>
<p> Primary Industries..........LIM Keng Yaik (GP)</p>
<p> Rural Development...........ANNUAR Musa (UMNO)</p>
<p> Science Technology &amp; Environment........LAW Hieng Ding (SUPP)</p>
<p>Transport..LING Liong Sik (MCA)</p>
<p> Works..........SAMY Vellu (MIC)</p>
<p> Youth &amp; Sports.........MUHYIDDIN Yassin (UMNO)</p>
<p>				- - - - - - -</p>
<p> Central Bank Governor........AHMAD Mohamed Don</p>
<p>				- - - - - - -</p>
<p>PARTY AFFILIATIONS:</p>
<p>GP   -- Gerekan Party (Parti Gerakan Rakyat Malaysia)</p>
<p>MCA  -- Malaysian Chinese Association</p>
<p>MIC  -- Malaysian Indian Congress</p>
<p>PBB -- Pesaka Bumiputra Bersatu Party</p>
<p>PBDS -- Bensa Dayak Sarawak Party</p>
<p>SUPP -- Sarawak United People's Party</p>
<p>UMNO -- New United Malays National Organisation</p>
<p>				  - - - - - - -</p>
